  ✓ Stage 2: check program fidelity and run independent differential tests
  ✓ Stage 3: rebuild definitions and reconstruct all positive proofs
  ✓ Stage 4: assess claim adequacy and real-program pinning
  → Stage 5: inventory and review every relevant K rule
  • Stage 6: run a fresh meaningful non-vacuity mutation
  • Stage 7: account for proven versus assumed boundaries and write REVIEW.md
